sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "lloyds", "sentiment": "none"}]}, "highlightText": "", "language": "english", "persons": [], "text": "Lenovo shares hit by Chinese spy chip fears More Investing.com - Shares in China’s Lenovo Group were down again on Monday after tumbling as much as 20% on Friday following a Bloomberg report that Chinese spies used microchips to hack into some U.S. companies’ systems.\nLenovo (HK:0992) shares were down 1.58% to HK$4.98 by 1:40AM ET (05:40 GMT).\nBloomberg Businessweek reported Friday that Chinese spies placed microchips inside equipment used by about 30 companies, including Amazon, Apple, a major bank, and government contractors, allegedly giving Beijing access to U.S. computer networks.\nLenovo shares plunged following the report, even after Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) and Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN) denied it.\nLenovo said in a statement that SuperMicro, cited in the Bloomberg report as the supplier of the chips, is not a supplier to the company.\nRelated Articles\nBritain's Schroders gains on potential Lloyds wealth deal\nPhilippines stocks lower at close of trade; PSEi Composite down 0.39%\nEuropean shares fall as risk-off sentiment spreads", "external_links": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/philippines-stocks-lower-at-close-of-trade-psei-composite-down-039-1635041?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/european-shares-fall-as-riskoff-sentiment-spreads-1635029?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/britains-schroders-gains-on-potential-lloyds-wealth-deal-1635052?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/philippines-stocks-lower-at-close-of-trade-psei-composite-down-039-1635041?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://s.yimg.com/ny